  "description": "Reid Blacktop 2 ST | Step-through electric urban bike\nMid-drive power. Everyday versatility.\nThe Reid Blacktop 2 ST is a step-through electric bike designed for urban commuting and everyday riding. Its refined frame and geometry improve stiffness and ride feel, while the alloy frame, internal cable routing and integrated 418Wh battery create a clean, streamlined design. The step-through frame makes getting on and off the bike easier.\nPowered by an Ananda M60 250W mid-drive motor delivering 70Nm of torque, the Blacktop 2 ST provides responsive assistance and efficient power delivery through the drivetrain. The integrated 36V 11.6Ah battery supports everyday journeys, while the Ananda D18 Bluetooth display provides clear ride data and smartphone app compatibility.\nThe Shimano Cues U4000 9-speed drivetrain combines a 9-speed shifter and rear derailleur with a Shimano Cues 11–46T cassette. This wide gear range offers flexibility across flat roads and steeper inclines. Tektro hydraulic disc brakes, with a 180mm front rotor and 160mm rear rotor, provide reliable braking performance.\nThe Blacktop 2 ST rolls on 27.5-inch wheels fitted with 2.1-inch tyres for a balance of traction, stability and comfort on urban roads. An enhanced City Sport saddle, ergonomic lock-on grips, oversized alloy handlebars and an adjustable riser stem complete the setup, allowing riders to fine-tune their riding position for everyday comfort.\nThe Reid Blacktop 2 ST is ideal for:\n\nEasy access – A step-through frame makes mounting and dismounting more convenient\n\nUrban commuting – Mid-drive assistance for everyday journeys\n\nHilly routes – 70Nm of torque and a wide-range 9-speed drivetrain\n\nEveryday versatility – 27.5-inch wheels and 2.1-inch tyres for varied urban surfaces\n\nReliable braking – Tektro hydraulic disc brakes with 180mm front and 160mm rear rotors\n\nComfort-focused riding – Comfort Plus saddle, ergonomic grips and adjustable riser stem\n\nConnected cycling – Ananda D18 Bluetooth display with app compatibility\n\nPlease make sure to familiarise yourself with eBike safety information before charging or using your new Reid. You can view and download user manuals and safety instructions here.",
